  "verbalization": "Tiapride is implicated in the target pathway leading to Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Tiapride interacts with 6-phosphofructo-2-kinase/fructose-2,6-bisphosphatase 4, which in turn is targeted by a second molecule, 4-Methyl-5-[(2Z)-2-{[4-(4-morpholinyl)phenyl]imino}-2,5-dihydro-4-pyrimidinyl]-1,3-thiazol-2-amine, and finally, Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Tiapride may influence the activity of the enzyme through a series of intermediate targets. The presence of multiple distinct targets suggests that Tiapride may act through different mechanisms, possibly by modulating the activity of various enzymes in the metabolic pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Tiapride and Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, emphasizing the role of intermediate targets in mediating the drug's effect.",
